/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 95 0 R
/T (Data integrity means the data in the database is accurate, consistent and valid at all times. Instead of trusting every application to check its input, the Airline Reservation System enforces its rules inside the database using constraints. This report lists the constraints implemented in airline_reservation_system.sql, explains why each one is needed, and describes the tests in data_integrity_tests.sql that verify them.)
/E (Data integrity means the data in the database is accurate, consistent and valid at all times. Instead of trusting every application to check its input, the Airline Reservation System enforces its rules inside the database using constraints. This report lists the constraints implemented in airline_reservation_system.sql, explains why each one is needed, and describes the tests in data_integrity_tests.sql that verify them.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
